# ShellCheck configuration for tests/ ONLY — scripts/ stays fully strict.
#
# SC2030 / SC2031 ("modified in a subshell"): the cases run helpers inside
# ( … ) subshells ON PURPOSE, so that sourcing scripts/_common.sh (which sets
# -euo pipefail and defines globals) cannot leak into the next assertion. The
# checks fire on exactly that intended pattern.
#
# SC2016 ("expressions don't expand in single quotes"): the runner passes shell
# snippets to `bash -c` as single-quoted literals, and several assertions look
# for literal '$' text (a cost of "$1.24", a template containing '${x}'). Every
# hit here is deliberate.
disable=SC2030,SC2031,SC2016
